---
// Homepage - v2 "editorial depth" skin on the approved wireframe structure.
// Copy is canon (PRD rule 6). Styles: src/styles/home.css, tokens only.
// v1 design export archived at design-briefs/styled-homepage-v1.html.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import '../styles/home.css';

// $97 session sells via the standalone landing page (decided 2026-07-12).
// Off-domain for now; swap to the on-domain "/session" port here when it ships.
const SESSION_URL = 'https://abq-landing-v2.vercel.app';
---

<Base
  title="Quit Smoking or Vaping With Always Be Quitting"
  description="Coaching and community from a certified tobacco treatment specialist with 25 years of experience."
>
  <!-- 0 · announcement + nav -->
  <SiteHeader />

  <!-- 1 · hero - HEADLINE + ONE LINE, NOTHING ELSE (Jon, 2026-08-14).
       Matches the live site exactly: no sub-headline, no trust line, no opt-in.
       Design phase: full-bleed environmental photograph, both lines on a scrim.
       "You've tried before" needs statement weight, not kicker size. -->
  <header class="band band--mist hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1 class="display-xl hl">
        Make This Your Last Attempt to Quit Smoking or Vaping, <em>Not Just Your Next One</em>
      </h1>
      <p class="kicker kicker--under">You've tried before. It didn't last.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <!-- 1b · Quick-Start Guide opt-in - its own section directly below the hero,
       per the live site. Moved out of the hero 2026-08-14. Band treatment TBD
       in the design phase (live site uses a sage field here). -->
  <section class="band band--paper optin-band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="optin reveal">
        <h3>Get Your Free Always Be Quitting "Quick-Start Guide"</h3>
        <p><em>Start breaking your smoking or vaping addiction in 20 minutes - even if you're not ready to quit yet.</em></p>
        <!-- Second line restored from the live site (typo "this this" fixed).
             It's the only copy that says what they actually receive: a video. -->
        <p><em>I use this simple technique with my clients and it works. You will receive a video about how and when to use it.</em></p>
        <!-- first_name added for email personalization. NOTE: /api/subscribe is an
             M3 task and must pass this through to systeme.io when it's built. -->
        <form action="/api/subscribe" method="post">
          <input type="text" name="first_name" placeholder="First name" required />
          <input type="email" name="email" placeholder="Your email" required />
          <button class="btn btn--cta" type="submit">Send me the free guide</button>
        </form>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2 · recognition -->
  <section class="band band--paper recognition">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="lead reveal">
        <h2 class="display-lg hl">You try to quit. It doesn't last. Months later you try again - <em>and the cycle repeats.</em></h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid--4">
        <div class="card reveal">
          <h3>You can't seem to start.</h3>
          <p>You know you want to quit. You've thought about it for months, maybe years. But the moment to actually do it never quite arrives.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card reveal">
          <h3>You're struggling to stay quit.</h3>
          <p>You made it a few days, weeks, or longer. But the cravings, the stress, the routines keep pulling you back, and you can feel yourself slipping.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card reveal">
          <h3>You've already quit and want it to last.</h3>
          <p>You stopped smoking or vaping, but you're worried about going back. You want to make sure it sticks this time.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card reveal">
          <h3>You've relapsed and want to try again.</h3>
          <p>It already happened. You're frustrated, tired of the cycle, and ready for something different. You want to try again, but smarter this time.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 3 · transformation -->
  <section class="band band--teal transform">
    <div class="wrap reveal">
      <h2 class="display-xl" style="margin-top:1.2rem">
        Temporary abstinence isn't quitting - <span class="sweep"><em>transformation is.</em></span>
      </h2>
      <p>
        Stopping can happen fast. Staying quit is a months-long transformation.
        That's why nothing here promises you'll quit in X days.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 4 · what makes the difference -->
  <section class="band band--white recognition" style="margin-top:0">
    <div class="wrap" style="padding-block: clamp(4.5rem, 9vw, 7rem) 0">
      <h2 class="display-lg hl" style="margin-top:1rem">Here's What Makes <em>The Difference</em></h2>
      <div class="grid grid--4" style="margin-block: 2.4rem 5rem">
        <div class="card card--pop reveal">
          <h3>Expert Guidance</h3>
          <p>from someone who knows the many paths to quitting</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card card--pop reveal">
          <h3>Real Accountability</h3>
          <p>when cravings hit and you want to give in</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card card--pop reveal">
          <h3>Ongoing Motivation</h3>
          <p>to keep you moving forward</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card card--pop reveal">
          <h3>Mindset Transformation</h3>
          <p>that helps you stay quit for life</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 5 · guide -->
  <section class="band band--white guide" style="padding-top:0">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="guide__row reveal">
        <div class="guide__photo">[ Jon - real photo coming ]</div>
        <div>
          <h2 class="display-lg">I'm Jon, and I provide exactly that kind of support.</h2>
          <p style="margin-top:1.2rem; color:var(--soft)">
            I know how discouraging your struggle is. I've spent 25 years helping people who thought they could
            never quit smoking or vaping - quit for life. And <em>I can help you, too.</em>
          </p>
          <p style="color:var(--soft); font-size:0.95rem">Get help from someone who has been successfully guiding people through quitting for decades.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="stats">
        <div class="stat reveal"><b>25 yrs</b><span>helping people quit smoking and vaping as a CTTS and NCNTT certified specialist</span></div>
        <div class="stat reveal"><b>3 decades</b><span>teaching informative, effective, and engaging health workshops</span></div>
        <div class="stat reveal"><b>35 yrs</b><span>creating programs that help people change their behavior</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 6a · WHAT JON OFFERS - the two levels of service, named plainly, no prices.
       Added 2026-08-14 (Jon). The old single "Start for $97" section was doing two
       jobs at once - announcing the offerings AND the entry price - so neither
       service registered and the page read as one product with two buttons.
       Offer-architecture rule 1: visitors self-select their level of service. -->
  <section class="band band--white offers">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="display-lg hl">Two ways to <em>work with me.</em></h2>
      <div class="grid grid--2">
        <div class="offer reveal">
          <h3>The ABQ Community</h3>
          <p>Weekly live Q&amp;A calls with Jon and 24/7 access to a community of people quitting alongside you. Move forward at your own pace, with support and accountability the whole way. You don't even have to be ready to quit to start.</p>
          <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/community">See how the community works</a>
        </div>
        <div class="offer reveal">
          <h3>1:1 Coaching</h3>
          <!-- Names that ongoing 1:1 work exists WITHOUT naming or pricing the
               $1,200 Program - keeps the 2026-07-12 PRD decision intact.
               Assembled from Jon's language: "Jon in your corner" (offer-architecture),
               "no one-size-fits-all programs" (trust line), relapse-as-path (FAQ voice). -->
          <p>Working with me directly, one to one, over the months a real transformation takes. Not a one-size-fits-all program - a plan built around your life, with me in your corner between sessions, for the slips as much as the wins.</p>
          <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/coaching">See how 1:1 coaching works</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 6b · HOW YOU START - the $97 entry into either one. Price lives here only.
       Both being $97 is deliberate and reads as generous once 6a has done the
       distinguishing. -->
  <section class="band band--paper band--dots doors">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="doors__mega reveal" aria-hidden="true">$97</div>
      <h2 class="display-lg hl">Either way, <em>you start for $97.</em></h2>
      <div class="grid grid--2">
        <div class="door door--community reveal">
          <h3>The ABQ Community</h3>
          <div class="price">$97/month</div>
          <p class="door__terms">3-month commitment, then just $47/month.</p>
          <a class="btn btn--cta" href="/community">Join the Community</a>
        </div>
        <div class="door door--session reveal">
          <h3>A 1:1 Session</h3>
          <div class="price">$97 one-time</div>
          <p class="door__terms">A focused 50-minute conversation, and where working together begins.</p>
          <a class="btn btn--cta" href={SESSION_URL}>Book your $97 session</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="doors__mitigate reveal">$97 is less than most people spend in a single month (or week) on smoking or vaping.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 7 · proof -->
  <section class="band band--white proof">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="grid grid--3" style="margin-top:2rem">
        <figure class="card quote reveal">
          <blockquote>Jon became my outlet, a safe person who helped me negotiate that struggle. The impact he has had on my life is transformative.</blockquote>
          <figcaption><b>Katherine R.</b> · One Year Vape Free</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="card quote reveal">
          <blockquote>He broke the all-or-nothing thinking for me. He came in with curiosity, just getting to understand where I was at, so that he could help me.</blockquote>
          <figcaption><b>Kait</b> · 9 Years Sober, Now Smoke-Free</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="card quote reveal">
          <blockquote>I've invited Jon to teach about tobacco treatment to my university class for 9 straight semesters… informative, entertaining and inspiring.</blockquote>
          <figcaption><b>Ashley Foster, MPH, RD, CHES</b> · University Professor</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FAQ section removed entirely (Jon, 2026-08-14). Objection-handling belongs
       on /community and /coaching, where the decision is actually made; the
       homepage had enough text. Nothing from it was relocated. -->


  <!-- 8b · STAKES - StoryBrand beat 7 (Failure), placed immediately before the
       final ask so the stakes land while the CTA is in view. Copy is Jon's,
       verbatim, approved 2026-08-14.
       NOTE: the "physically and mentally sick" sentence is a deliberate,
       Jon-approved exception to the voice.md DON'T "fear-of-death or
       medical-scare messaging." Recorded in voice.md - do not "fix" it. -->
  <section class="band band--white stakes">
    <div class="wrap reveal">
      <p class="display-lg stakes__body">
        You can continue to spend $1k, $2k, $3k, $4k every year on cigarettes and vapes.
        You can continue to make yourself physically and mentally sick.
        And next year at this time, you'll wish you had started today.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 9 · final cta -->
  <section class="band band--navy final">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="display-xl hl">Always be quitting, <em>until you've quit for the last time.</em></h2>
      <div class="final__actions reveal">
        <a class="btn btn--cta" href="/community">Join the Community</a>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href={SESSION_URL}>Book a $97 Session</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 10 · footer -->
  <SiteFooter />
</Base>
